{
 "chapter": 1,
 "title": "What \u201cinvestment\u201d actually means",
 "duration": 150.2666666666657,
 "cues": [
  {
   "start": 6.333333333333329,
   "end": 11.92367346938775,
   "text": "Start with the simplest picture there is. A factory. Nell's factory.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 12.333333333333321,
   "end": 18.747891156462572,
   "text": "Every month, money comes in. Customers buy what she makes, and they pay her.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 20.86666666666664,
   "end": 27.85229024943308,
   "text": "Economists call that revenue. All the money coming in, before anything is taken out of it.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 30.5333333333333,
   "end": 39.351156462585,
   "text": "Every month, money also goes out. She pays for materials, for electricity, for wages, for the rent.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 41.53333333333344,
   "end": 45.64911564625861,
   "text": "cost. All the money going out to keep the place running.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 48.13333333333346,
   "end": 52.655464852607835,
   "text": "The difference between the two is what she actually keeps.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 54.80000000000033,
   "end": 58.9595464852611,
   "text": "profit. Revenue minus cost. What is left over.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 63.20000000000044,
   "end": 70.96739229024988,
   "text": "Not all costs behave the same way. The rent is the same whether she makes one chair or a thousand.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 73.13333333333367,
   "end": 77.85446712018174,
   "text": "fixed cost. A cost that does not change with how much you make.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 80.2000000000003,
   "end": 86.7928798185944,
   "text": "The wood is different. Make twice as many chairs and she buys twice as much wood.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 88.93333333333338,
   "end": 94.34761904761909,
   "text": "variable cost. A cost that rises and falls with how much you make.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 98.99999999999989,
   "end": 104.48235827664388,
   "text": "You may think investment means buying shares in a company. That is not what an economist means by it.",
   "voice": "c"
  },
  {
   "start": 104.86666666666649,
   "end": 112.51487528344653,
   "text": "It means this. You spend a large sum of money now, to build something that will produce revenue later.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 114.66666666666617,
   "end": 120.60997732426254,
   "text": "investment. Spending a large sum now to build something that earns later.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 123.66666666666615,
   "end": 134.64943310657543,
   "text": "A factory. A shop fitted out. A well drilled. A machine bought. That is investment, and that is the decision this whole film is about.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 137.5333333333326,
   "end": 140.87124716553214,
   "text": "revenue \u2212 cost = profit",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 140.9999999999992,
   "end": 143.908344671201,
   "text": "fixed stays put \u00b7 variable moves",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 143.99999999999915,
   "end": 148.03451247165447,
   "text": "investment = spend now, earn later",
   "voice": "n"
  }
 ],
